{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"agent_message","text":"A stride-alignment pad helps the power-of-two `time=8192` case, but profiling points to the bigger issue: the first kernel traverses weights at stride 5 for each tap. I’m changing the reduction to the weights’ native contiguous `(channel, tap)` order; this should remove gather-heavy matrix loads without altering the convolution."}}
